    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "544A Delegation of Director’s functions or powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-1-sec-544a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director of Human Biosecurity may, in writing, delegate any\nor all of the Director’s functions or powers under this Act to an\nSES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Health\nDepartment.\nNote 1:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nSee also sections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nwhich contain extra rules about delegations.\n(2) The functions or powers that may be delegated under\nsubsection (1) include functions or powers the Director of Human\nBiosecurity has as an authorised applicant or authorised person for\nthe purposes of a provision of the Regulatory Powers Act because\nof this Act.\n(3) However, the Director of Human Biosecurity must not delegate the\nDirector’s functions or powers under any of the following\nprovisions:\n(a) section 113 (human health response zones);\n(b) section 570 (issuing identity cards);\n(c) section 618 (declared movements).\n(4) Also, the Director of Human Biosecurity may delegate a function\nor power under Part 3 of Chapter 2 (human biosecurity control\norders) only to an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in\nthe Health Department who is a human biosecurity officer.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendment of the Biosecurity Act 2015  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(5) A human biosecurity officer cannot, under a delegation to which\nsubsection (4) applies, perform a function or exercise a power\nunder section 72 in relation to a human biosecurity control order if\nthe human biosecurity officer:\n(a) imposed the order under paragraph 60(1)(b); or\n(b) made the request under subsection 71(3) in relation to the\norder.\n(6) In performing any functions or exercising any powers under a\ndelegation made under subsection (1), the delegate must comply\nwith any directions of the Director of Human Biosecurity.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director of Human Biosecurity may, in writing, delegate any\nor all of the Director’s functions or powers under this Act to an\nSES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Health\nDepartment.\nNote 1:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nSee also sections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nwhich contain extra rules about delegations.\n(2) The functions or powers that may be delegated under\nsubsection (1) include functions or powers the Director of Human\nBiosecurity has as an authorised applicant or authorised person for\nthe purposes of a provision of the Regulatory Powers Act because\nof this Act.\n(3) However, the Director of Human Biosecurity must not delegate the\nDirector’s functions or powers under any of the following\nprovisions:\n(a) section 113 (human health response zones);\n(b) section 570 (issuing identity cards);\n(c) section 618 (declared movements).\n(4) Also, the Director of Human Biosecurity may delegate a function\nor power under Part 3 of Chapter 2 (human biosecurity control\norders) only to an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in\nthe Health Department who is a human biosecurity officer.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendment of the Biosecurity Act 2015  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(5) A human biosecurity officer cannot, under a delegation to which\nsubsection (4) applies, perform a function or exercise a power\nunder section 72 in relation to a human biosecurity control order if\nthe human biosecurity officer:\n(a) imposed the order under paragraph 60(1)(b); or\n(b) made the request under subsection 71(3) in relation to the\norder.\n(6) In performing any functions or exercising any powers under a\ndelegation made under subsection (1), the delegate must comply\nwith any directions of the Director of Human Biosecurity.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-1-sec-544a-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6e905fa50ed340846326fd7db8fdfccdc81f431483b160b392d42b51a28febd1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-1-sec-544a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "544A Delegation of Director’s functions or powers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director of Human Biosecurity may, in writing, delegate any\nor all of the Director’s functions or powers under this Act to an\nSES employee, or an acting SES employee, in the Health\nDepartment.\nNote 1:\nThe expressions SES employee and acting SES employee are defined\nin section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nNote 2:\nSee also sections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901,\nwhich contain extra rules about delegations.\n(2) The functions or powers that may be delegated under\nsubsection (1) include functions or powers the Director of Human\nBiosecurity has as an authorised applicant or authorised person for\nthe purposes of a provision of the Regulatory Powers Act because\nof this Act.\n(3) However, the Director of Human Biosecurity must not delegate the\nDirector’s functions or powers under any of the following\nprovisions:\n(a) section 113 (human health response zones);\n(b) section 570 (issuing identity cards);\n(c) section 618 (declared movements).\n(4) Also, the Director of Human Biosecurity may delegate a function\nor power under Part 3 of Chapter 2 (human biosecurity control\norders) only to an SES employee, or an acting SES employee, in\nthe Health Department who is a human biosecurity officer.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendment of the Biosecurity Act 2015  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(5) A human biosecurity officer cannot, under a delegation to which\nsubsection (4) applies, perform a function or exercise a power\nunder section 72 in relation to a human biosecurity control order if\nthe human biosecurity officer:\n(a) imposed the order under paragraph 60(1)(b); or\n(b) made the request under subsection 71(3) in relation to the\norder.\n(6) In performing any functions or exercising any powers under a\ndelegation made under subsection (1), the delegate must comply\nwith any directions of the Director of Human Biosecurity."
    },
