    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Transitional—transfer of documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director-General of the\nCDC under:\n(i) the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025; or\n(ii) the Biosecurity Act 2015; or\n(iii) the National Health Security Act 2007; or\n(iv) the National Occupational Respiratory Disease Registry\nAct 2023; and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Health Secretary; or\n(ii) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(iii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iv) a delegate of the Health Secretary or the\nCommonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Director-General\nof the CDC after the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the\nDirector-General of the CDC.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director-General of the\nCDC under:\n(i) the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025; or\n(ii) the Biosecurity Act 2015; or\n(iii) the National Health Security Act 2007; or\n(iv) the National Occupational Respiratory Disease Registry\nAct 2023; and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Health Secretary; or\n(ii) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(iii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iv) a delegate of the Health Secretary or the\nCommonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Director-General\nof the CDC after the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the\nDirector-General of the CDC.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f2a34f722318c915f21d5b3684dafed7e131c6f0998427174a84820e94cd645",
      "skos:note": "Transfer records and documents to Director-General of CDC after transition time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Transitional—transfer of documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director-General of the\nCDC under:\n(i) the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025; or\n(ii) the Biosecurity Act 2015; or\n(iii) the National Health Security Act 2007; or\n(iv) the National Occupational Respiratory Disease Registry\nAct 2023; and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Health Secretary; or\n(ii) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(iii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iv) a delegate of the Health Secretary or the\nCommonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Director-General\nof the CDC after the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the\nDirector-General of the CDC.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025"
    },
