    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Enterprise Agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, at and from the transition time, to cover and apply\nto APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ntransition time; and\n(ii) who, at the transition time, are members of the staff of\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the Department of Health and\nAged Care Enterprise Agreement whose employment as a\nmember of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease\nControl commences at or after the transition time.\n(2)\nAt and after the transition time, the Department of Health and Aged\nCare Enterprise Agreement covers and applies to the Director-General\nof the CDC as the Agency Head of the APS employees who are\nmembers of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the\nDepartment of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement in\naccordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control from being varied at or after the transition time:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, at and from the transition time, to cover and apply\nto APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ntransition time; and\n(ii) who, at the transition time, are members of the staff of\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the Department of Health and\nAged Care Enterprise Agreement whose employment as a\nmember of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease\nControl commences at or after the transition time.\n(2)\nAt and after the transition time, the Department of Health and Aged\nCare Enterprise Agreement covers and applies to the Director-General\nof the CDC as the Agency Head of the APS employees who are\nmembers of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the\nDepartment of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement in\naccordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control from being varied at or after the transition time:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ed4ccb70ca316d2b1e88f1131ad1ccef20ef958a583441ac36329ba472d828c",
      "skos:note": "Continues and applies to APS employees, including those at the Australian Centre for Disease Control."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Enterprise Agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, at and from the transition time, to cover and apply\nto APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ntransition time; and\n(ii) who, at the transition time, are members of the staff of\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the Department of Health and\nAged Care Enterprise Agreement whose employment as a\nmember of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease\nControl commences at or after the transition time.\n(2)\nAt and after the transition time, the Department of Health and Aged\nCare Enterprise Agreement covers and applies to the Director-General\nof the CDC as the Agency Head of the APS employees who are\nmembers of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the\nDepartment of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement in\naccordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control from being varied at or after the transition time:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements."
    },
