    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Transitional rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Health Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n(a) required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Act.\n(2)\nWithout limiting subitem (1), the rules may prescribe matters of a\ntransitional nature (including prescribing any saving or application\nprovisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nAct 2025.\n(3)\nWithout limiting subitem (2), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubitem before the end of the period of 12 months starting at the\ntransition time may modify the operation of the provisions of this Act or\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 or any other Act or\ninstrument.\n(4)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act or the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control Act 2025.\n(5)\nThis Schedule (other than subitem (4)) does not limit the rules that may\nbe made for the purposes of subitem (1).\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe Health Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n(a) required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Act.\n(2)\nWithout limiting subitem (1), the rules may prescribe matters of a\ntransitional nature (including prescribing any saving or application\nprovisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nAct 2025.\n(3)\nWithout limiting subitem (2), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubitem before the end of the period of 12 months starting at the\ntransition time may modify the operation of the provisions of this Act or\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 or any other Act or\ninstrument.\n(4)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act or the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control Act 2025.\n(5)\nThis Schedule (other than subitem (4)) does not limit the rules that may\nbe made for the purposes of subitem (1).\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1302cb16034f3982fe01e84cb580a0d1d2c106bc86e76278cbe2aedca7756bd8",
      "skos:note": "The Health Minister may make rules prescribing matters related to the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Transitional rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Health Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nprescribing matters:\n(a) required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed by the\nrules; or\n(b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or\ngiving effect to this Act.\n(2)\nWithout limiting subitem (1), the rules may prescribe matters of a\ntransitional nature (including prescribing any saving or application\nprovisions) relating to:\n(a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or\n(b) the enactment of the Australian Centre for Disease Control\nAct 2025.\n(3)\nWithout limiting subitem (2), rules made for the purposes of that\nsubitem before the end of the period of 12 months starting at the\ntransition time may modify the operation of the provisions of this Act or\nthe Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 or any other Act or\ninstrument.\n(4)\nTo avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following:\n(a) create an offence or civil penalty;\n(b) provide powers of:\n(i) arrest or detention; or\n(ii) entry, search or seizure;\n(c) impose a tax;\n(d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated\nRevenue Fund;\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nGeneral provisions  Part 1\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\n(e) directly amend the text of this Act or the Australian Centre\nfor Disease Control Act 2025.\n(5)\nThis Schedule (other than subitem (4)) does not limit the rules that may\nbe made for the purposes of subitem (1).\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
