      "cml:conclusionText": "(2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Transitional—transfer of documents to Health Secretary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director of Human\nBiosecurity under the Biosecurity Act 2015 (other than\nsection 42 or 169 of that Act); and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(ii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iii) a delegate of the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Health Secretary\nafter the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the Director of\nHuman Biosecurity.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director of Human\nBiosecurity under the Biosecurity Act 2015 (other than\nsection 42 or 169 of that Act); and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(ii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iii) a delegate of the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Health Secretary\nafter the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the Director of\nHuman Biosecurity.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-9-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "191cf7ee9f360d6dce22b565e622194bd26bd79da970bef7df018da5f18f8642",
      "skos:note": "Transfer of documents to Health Secretary after transition time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Transitional—transfer of documents to Health Secretary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to any records or documents that:\n(a) relate to a function or power of the Director of Human\nBiosecurity under the Biosecurity Act 2015 (other than\nsection 42 or 169 of that Act); and\n(b) immediately before the transition time, were in the\npossession of:\n(i) the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer; or\n(ii) an APS employee in the Health Department; or\n(iii) a delegate of the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe records and documents are to be transferred to the Health Secretary\nafter the transition time.\nNote:\nAny records and documents transferred are Commonwealth records for the purposes of\nthe Archives Act 1983.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that:\n(a) subitem (2) does not apply to specified records or documents;\nor\n(b) subitem (2) does not apply to records or documents that\nrelate to a specified function or power of the Director of\nHuman Biosecurity.\n(4)\nSubitem (3) does not limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901."
    },
    {
