      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Things done before transition time.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subitem (1) does not apply in relation to specified thing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 References to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "instruments\n(1)\nThis item applies to an instrument if:\n(a) the instrument was made under the old NORDR Act; and\n(b) the instrument was in force immediately before the transition\ntime; and\n(c) the instrument contains a reference to the Commonwealth\nChief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe instrument has effect, at and after the transition time, as if a\nreference in the instrument to the Commonwealth Chief Medical\nOfficer were a reference to the Director-General of the CDC.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that subitem (2) does not apply in\nrelation to a specified instrument or a specified reference.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the instrument from being amended or\nrepealed after the commencement of this item.\n(5)\nIn this item:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nProvisions relating to the amendment of the National Occupational Respiratory Disease\nRegistry Act 2023  Part 4\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\ninstrument includes:\n(a) a contract, deed, undertaking, arrangement or agreement; and\n(b) a notice, authority, order or instruction; and\n(c) an instrument made under the old NORDR Act or rules made\nunder the old NORDR Act.",
      "skos:definition": "instruments\n(1)\nThis item applies to an instrument if:\n(a) the instrument was made under the old NORDR Act; and\n(b) the instrument was in force immediately before the transition\ntime; and\n(c) the instrument contains a reference to the Commonwealth\nChief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe instrument has effect, at and after the transition time, as if a\nreference in the instrument to the Commonwealth Chief Medical\nOfficer were a reference to the Director-General of the CDC.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that subitem (2) does not apply in\nrelation to a specified instrument or a specified reference.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the instrument from being amended or\nrepealed after the commencement of this item.\n(5)\nIn this item:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nProvisions relating to the amendment of the National Occupational Respiratory Disease\nRegistry Act 2023  Part 4\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\ninstrument includes:\n(a) a contract, deed, undertaking, arrangement or agreement; and\n(b) a notice, authority, order or instruction; and\n(c) an instrument made under the old NORDR Act or rules made\nunder the old NORDR Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0c48edfe5409059e042e6d70e7c479128be1603ffc4df6698f0610ec72686c3a",
      "skos:note": "References to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer in instruments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 References to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "instruments\n(1)\nThis item applies to an instrument if:\n(a) the instrument was made under the old NORDR Act; and\n(b) the instrument was in force immediately before the transition\ntime; and\n(c) the instrument contains a reference to the Commonwealth\nChief Medical Officer.\n(2)\nThe instrument has effect, at and after the transition time, as if a\nreference in the instrument to the Commonwealth Chief Medical\nOfficer were a reference to the Director-General of the CDC.\n(3)\nThe transitional rules may provide that subitem (2) does not apply in\nrelation to a specified instrument or a specified reference.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the instrument from being amended or\nrepealed after the commencement of this item.\n(5)\nIn this item:\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nProvisions relating to the amendment of the National Occupational Respiratory Disease\nRegistry Act 2023  Part 4\nNo. 62, 2025\nAustralian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments\nand Transitional Provisions) Act 2025\ninstrument includes:\n(a) a contract, deed, undertaking, arrangement or agreement; and\n(b) a notice, authority, order or instruction; and\n(c) an instrument made under the old NORDR Act or rules made\nunder the old NORDR Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-16-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies references to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The instrument contains a reference to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The instrument has effect, at and after the transition time, as if a reference in the instrument to the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer were a reference to the Director-General of the CDC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Legal proceedings involving the Commonwealth Chief",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2025a00062.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2025a00062.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "Medical Officer or Health Secretary\n(1)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer was a party to proceedings relating to the old NORDR\nAct that were pending in any court or tribunal, the Director-General of\nthe CDC is substituted for the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer as\na party to the proceedings at and after that time.\n(2)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Health Secretary was a\nparty to proceedings relating to the old NORDR Act that were pending\nin any court or tribunal, the Director-General of the CDC is substituted\nfor the Health Secretary as a party to the proceedings at and after that\ntime.\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 3 September 2025\nSenate on 27 October 2025]\n(69/25)",
      "skos:definition": "Medical Officer or Health Secretary\n(1)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer was a party to proceedings relating to the old NORDR\nAct that were pending in any court or tribunal, the Director-General of\nthe CDC is substituted for the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer as\na party to the proceedings at and after that time.\n(2)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Health Secretary was a\nparty to proceedings relating to the old NORDR Act that were pending\nin any court or tribunal, the Director-General of the CDC is substituted\nfor the Health Secretary as a party to the proceedings at and after that\ntime.\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 3 September 2025\nSenate on 27 October 2025]\n(69/25)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a9a3abf06efb37aaf3f2ae4c6f91c50e65e89e37a3ddba88cc83dfd9a3e49f4",
      "skos:note": "Substitution of Director-General for Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer and Health Secretary in pending proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2025a00062#sch-2-sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Legal proceedings involving the Commonwealth Chief",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "Medical Officer or Health Secretary\n(1)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Commonwealth Chief\nMedical Officer was a party to proceedings relating to the old NORDR\nAct that were pending in any court or tribunal, the Director-General of\nthe CDC is substituted for the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer as\na party to the proceedings at and after that time.\n(2)\nIf, immediately before the transition time, the Health Secretary was a\nparty to proceedings relating to the old NORDR Act that were pending\nin any court or tribunal, the Director-General of the CDC is substituted\nfor the Health Secretary as a party to the proceedings at and after that\ntime.\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 3 September 2025\nSenate on 27 October 2025]\n(69/25)"
    },
    {
